    "description": "The Broadband Infrared Radiometer (BBIR) is a modified instrument for airborne use to measure net irradiance, radiative forcing, absorption, and albedo. These data were collected aboard the DC-8 research aircraft during the Tropical Composition, Cloud, and Climate Coupling (TC4) field campaign. This field campaign took place in the tropical Eastern Pacific and Caribbean Sea with the primary goal to better understand the role that the tropical tropopause layer (TTL) plays in Earth\u2019s climate and atmospheric chemistry. These files are available in ASCII text file format divided between vertical and horizontal probe channels. These data were collected between June 28, 2007 through August 10, 2007 and are available in ASCII format.",
